description:
The CMS Acquisition Lifecycle Management (CALM) is an application for OAGM, OFM, and Program Offices to utilize for executing the various points of the acquisition lifecycle.  CALM modernizes collaboration with internal and external stakeholders, improve procurement decision making, and centralize silo systems and processes into one modern and efficient application. This shall be achieved through the implementation of an agile IT development process that focuses results on continuous capability enhancements, minimal downtime, prompt response to emerging needs, demonstrated reliability and system sustainability, and optimized performance with resource utilization minimized. The CALM application is an acquisition system that will improve procurement decision making by achieving the following CMS stated Program Goals:
 Goal 1-Drive all contract planning through CALM (Centralize all contracting activities);
 Goal 2-Ensure contract compliance with all statutory, regulatory, and policy requirements;
 Goal 3-Establish a single-source of truth for acquisition data;
 Goal 4-Maximize ability to recover/repurpose/eliminate ULOs (funds); and
 Goal 5-Reduce manual processing within acquisition lifecycle.
